+---
+id: dl-003-json-patch-values-must-be-json-values
+type: decision-log
+title: "JSON Patch values must be JSON values"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# JSON Patch values must be JSON values
+
+## Context
+RFC 6902 patches are JSON documents (section 3), so an operation `value` is a JSON value (RFC 8259).
+`applyPatch` only checked that `value` was present, so non-JSON values were accepted.
+
+## Decision
+`validateOperation` rejects a `value` that is not null, boolean, string, finite number, array or plain
+object (recursively, without cycles). This applies to `add`, `replace` and `test`.
+
+## Consequences
+Such patches now throw "Invalid JSON Patch" before any operation runs, rather than producing results
+that cannot be serialised as JSON. Complements dl-002.
